<section class="hero">
<div>
<p class="kicker">Dependency behavior receipt, live through plimsoll</p>
<h1>You installed a package. Here is what its code did, signed and tied to the run that installed it.</h1>
<p class="lede">Installing a package with npm, the package manager for Node.js (a JavaScript runtime), runs the package's <dfn>install script</dfn>, a command its <code>package.json</code> names (such as <code>postinstall</code>) that npm runs on the machine doing the install (<a href="https://docs.npmjs.com/cli/v10/using-npm/scripts">npm's scripts guide (EXTERNAL · official docs ↗)</a>). Importing the package runs its code again. Nothing in the install's output says what that code did. On this page plimsoll ran three installs, each in its own fresh <a href="../../trainers/glossary.html#sandbox">sandbox (INTERNAL · glossary →)</a> under <a href="../../trainers/glossary.html#gvisor">gVisor (INTERNAL · glossary →)</a>, and for each one signed a <dfn>receipt</dfn>: what the programs in that sandbox did, read from outside it, and which run it was.</p>
</div>
