<p>The receipts and logs are gzip-compressed. The receipt command reads a log either way and a receipt only as written. From the repository root:</p>
<pre>go run ./examples/dependency-receipt/live -verify     # this page's files, offline: starts nothing
gunzip -k docs/examples/dependency-receipt/receipts/network.intoto.json.gz
go run ./examples/dependency-receipt -check docs/examples/dependency-receipt/receipts/network.intoto.json \
    -pub docs/examples/dependency-receipt/harness.pub -log docs/examples/dependency-receipt/logs/network.boot.json.gz \
    -bundle docs/examples/dependency-receipt/bundle.jsonl -line {{.Network.Line}}</pre>
<p><code>-verify</code> checks the bundle's signatures and chain, checks every receipt against its log and record, requires both changed inputs and the wrong record to be refused, and requires this page to be exactly what <code>evidence.json</code> renders. Running everything again needs a kind cluster with agent-sandbox and the <code>{{.Ev.Cluster.RuntimeClass}}</code> runtime class: <code>go run ./examples/dependency-receipt/live</code> makes a Kubernetes namespace (a named group of the cluster's objects) of its own and deletes it after.</p>

